# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights in the audiobook-center React application following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights@^1.3.1` package to project dependencies
- Updated `package-lock.json` to reflect the new dependency and its sub-dependencies

### 2. Modified Files
- **src/App.jsx**: Added Speed Insights integration
  - Imported `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component after the Routes section, before the closing fragment tag
  - This ensures Speed Insights tracks all route navigations in the application

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for React applications (Create React App / Vite). The `SpeedInsights` component:
- Is a wrapper around the tracking script
- Provides seamless integration with React
- Automatically tracks route changes and performance metrics
- Will be initialized when the app is deployed to Vercel

## Build Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ All dependencies installed correctly
✅ Code changes are minimal and non-breaking
✅ Existing functionality preserved

## Next Steps for Deployment

Once this is deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Speed Insights tab)
2. After deployment, the `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` script will be available
3. Performance metrics will start being collected automatically
4. Data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights tab

## Files Modified
- `Frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `Frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `Frontend/src/App.jsx` - Added SpeedInsights component
